      "license": "AGPL-3.0-only",
      "testOnly": true,
      "rationale": "A second implementation of the `s.fem.fem2d` model and all twenty-five typed mutations, in Python, at `../../../../../🧪️tests/mutate-fem2d-1/🐍️component.py`. Written from `../🧬️schema/📸️snapshot/🔣️component.json` (the nine members and the analysis settings record), `../🧬️schema/🧬️mutations/📝️text/📖️component.grammar.semio` (the twenty-five verbs) and the twenty-five committed `(before, mutation, after, outcome)` specification vectors — which is also where the RECORD shapes and the cascade rules are actually written down. It imports nothing from this repository and transliterates none of its Rust. A third-party library was declined, not merely absent: `code_aster`, `OpenSees`, `anastruct` and `PyNite` compute displacements and forces FROM a model, while every one of the twenty-five kinds edits the model document itself — `replace-section` swaps a profile record, `add-load` appends to a case's load list, `change-load-case-self-weight` flips a boolean — and none of them reads `.dsl.semio`. DEFECT FOUND WHILE WRITING IT, reported rather than worked around: `../🧬️schema/🧬️mutations/🔣️component.json` is a verbatim copy of the SNAPSHOT schema with the title changed, and in the snapshot schema every one of `FemNode`, `FemElement`, `FemRegion`, `FemMaterial`, `FemSection`, `FemSupport`, `FemLoadCase` and `FemCombination` is an EMPTY object with no properties at all. `package` is deliberately empty: the implementation needs no distribution, so this entry contributes nothing to `🔒️dependencies.json`."
    }
  ],
